{"type":"text","timestamp":1788501514723,"sessionID":"ses_f95091285ffeUyOPTKkCcTTMx7","part":{"id":"prt_06aff38ae001gzpEPceTS46zwu","messageID":"msg_06aff196b001biJV5UvMPmn2ml","sessionID":"ses_f95091285ffeUyOPTKkCcTTMx7","type":"text","text":"Done. Summary of changes:\n\n**Core fix — dvc/fs/dvc.py:86-152**\n- `_DVCFileSystem.__init__` now takes a single `repo` param typed `str | os.PathLike | Repo` (replacing both `url` and the old `Repo`-typed `repo` params)\n- A `Repo` instance is stored directly (`self._repo`) without spawning a new repo connection; a string/PathLike is `os.fspath()`-ed into `_repo_kwargs[\"url\"]` — rev, subrepos, config, remote, and remote_config handling unchanged\n- Backward compat: the legacy `url=` keyword is still honored via `kwargs.get(\"url\")`, alongside the existing `fo` fallback\n- Docstring updated to reflect the unified `repo` parameter\n\n**Consistency — dvc/dependency/repo.py:157**: `RepoDependency._make_fs` now passes `repo=self.def_repo[self.PARAM_URL]` instead of `url=`\n\n**Tests**: updated `dvc/testing/api_tests.py` parametrization to `repo=` (keeping a `url=` case for backward compat), added `test_init_arg` covering positional/`repo=`/`url=`/`Repo`-instance variants in tests/unit/fs/test_dvc.py and test_dvcfs.py\n\n**Verification**: 140 unit fs tests, 24 dependency tests, 34 API func tests (incl. the new `local_url` case) all pass; only failure (`test_show.py::test_params_show_while_running_stage`) is pre-existing on a clean checkout. Also manually confirmed the actual goal works end-to-end: `url_to_fs(\"dvc://data/foo\", repo=\"/path/to/repo\", rev=\"HEAD\")` returns a working DVCFileSystem with `exists`/`open`/`isdvc` all functional.","time":{"start":1788501506222,"end":1788501514719}}}
